{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Yang2015-blue",
  "Source": "C. Yang, W. Shen, Y. Zhang, K. Li, X. Fang, X. Zhang, and X. Liu, \"Compact Multilayer Film Structure for Angle Insensitive Color Filtering,\" Sci. Rep. 5, 9285 (2015). doi:10.1038/srep09285 - Table 1 p. 3 (BLUE column); stack order from Fig. 1(a) and Methods p. 4",
  "Notes": "Reflective blue colour filter (asymmetric Cr/a-Si/Ag cavity with TiO2 antireflection overlayer), angle insensitive\nSpecification: High reflectance in the blue, low reflectance over green and red; colour unchanged with angle up to 50 deg (unpolarised).\nReported: Fig. 1(d), normal incidence, simulated curve read from the plot (approximate): R ~67 % from 410 to ~430 nm, ~42 % at 505 nm, ~20 % at ~550 nm, ~1 % from ~630 to 700 nm; measured ~56 % at 410-440 nm. Fig. 2(a): simulated peak ~66 % at 0 deg, decreasing to ~55-60 % at 50 deg, long-wave reflectance staying below ~5 %. Fig. 4(a): 150 C simulated ~70 % at 400 nm. Phase analysis (Fig. 3) at 409 nm for air/Cr/a-Si/Ag (TiO2 left out); critical angle in a-Si quoted as 14 deg.\nNotes: Table 1 lists layers from the substrate up; reversed here (TiO2 next to air). Ag > 100 nm, opaque, taken as substrate. a-Si index at 150 C (Fig. 1(b)) is plotted only; library 'a-Si' used. Cr 22 nm as printed in Table 1 (the pdf text layer agrees). Cr, Ag, TiO2 data not given. Unpolarised light; reference_nm arbitrary.\nLayers from Table 1 p. 3 (BLUE column); stack order from Fig. 1(a) and Methods p. 4; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R max 65.2 % at 401 nm in 400-450 nm (library a-Si, Cr, Ag, TiO2); paper R ~67 % at 410-430 nm (read off the plot; 150 C a-Si). Library a-Si (Pierce & Spicer) in place of the paper’s 150 C a-Si, which it gives only as a plot.",
